o interfere with a ballot’s return to the local elections official.\n\nThis bill would additionally make it a misdemeanor for any person having charge of a vote by mail ballot to interfere, as defined, with a ballot’s delivery to a voter. The bill would make it a felony for a person with authority to direct one or more persons subject to their supervision or authority to interfere with a ballot’s return to the local elections official or delivery to a voter. By expanding the scope of an existing crime, this bill would impose a state-mandated local program.\n\nThe California Constitution requires the state to reimburse local agencies and school districts for certain costs mandated by the state. Statutory provisions establish procedures for making that reimbursement.\n\nThis bill would provide that no reimbursement is required by this act for a specified reason.\n\nThis bill would declare that it is to take effect immediately as an urgency statute.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"immediate_effect_flag","date":"2026-09-19","note":"The official bill data flags this measure as taking immediate effect. The date shown is the day it was chaptered by the Secretary of State; individual provisions may state other operative dates."},"expiryClauses":[],"firstObservedAt":"2026-11-20T01:12:59Z","id":"ca-20252026-sb259","identifier":"SB 259","indicators":{"Appropriation":"NO","BudgetBill":"NO","Election":"NO","FiscalCommittee":"YES","ImmediateEffect":"YES","LocalProgram":"YES","TaxLevy":"NO","Urgency":"YES","UsualCurrentExpenses":"NO","VoteRequired":"TWO_THIRDS"},"introducedDate":"2025-02-03","issueTags":[{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"official subject line","matchedText":"Elections: vote by mail ballots.","ruleId":"tag-mail-2","tag":"mail-voting"}],"judicialNote":"Legislative status does not show whether a court has blocked, narrowed or upheld any provision. Check the linked litigation, which may be incomplete.","lastActionDate":"2026-09-19","last